  "howTo": {
   "goal": "Checkmate the other king: attack it so that it has no safe square to escape to.",
   "turn": [
    [
     "♟",
     "Pick a piece",
     "Tap one of your pieces. The squares it can move to light up (rings mean a capture)."
    ],
    [
     "🎯",
     "Move it",
     "Tap a highlighted square. Pawns reaching the far side choose a new piece."
    ],
    [
     "♚",
     "Special moves",
     "Castling (move the king two squares toward a rook) and en passant are supported automatically."
    ],
    [
     "½",
     "Draws",
     "Stalemate, threefold repetition, the fifty-move rule and bare kings end the game in a draw. You can also offer a draw, or resign."
    ]
   ],
   "tips": [
    "Colours are drawn at random. White moves first.",
    "The host picks the clock in the lobby. Your time only runs on your turn, White’s starts after the first move, and each move can add a few bonus seconds. Run out and you lose (it’s a draw if your opponent can’t possibly checkmate).",
    "The captured-pieces row shows who is ahead in material.",
    "Add a computer player to practise. The host picks its level in the lobby, from Easy up to Master."
   ]
  },
